{
 "esm": "0.8.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "ISRM_clean",
  "description": "FULLY-AUTOMATIC clean full-domain InMAP ISRM. Full-domain SR[src_cells, rcv_cells] per pathway AND per SR emission layer, E as the emission->(cell, layer) binning +-aggregate, X/Y as an in-model Lambert-conformal PROJECTION observed over raw emis_lon/emis_lat (the inline trig IS the lambert_conformal_forward_x/y expansion), projected at BUILD time by the general-eval coordinate path. PLUME RISE IS STATED HERE, NOT IN A RUNNER: eleven observeds carry ctessum/atmos ASMEPrecomputed + InMAP's findLayer over the zarr's own per-cell meteorology, and decide which of the three SR emission layers each record's plume reaches before the contraction. NO hand-authored pushdown constructs (no derived set / producer / member_factor) and NO caller-supplied projected coordinates. Builds with pushdown_rewrite=true: the auto-rewrite generates the support set + distinct producer + member_factor + gated_select, and the three gated SR providers are fetched pre-sliced to the invented source cells.",
  "authors": [
   "EarthSciML"
  ],
  "license": "MIT",
  "created": "2026-07-19T00:00:00Z",
  "tags": [
   "isrm",
   "plume_rise",
   "meteorology",
   "inmap",
   "source_receptor",
   "air_quality",
   "pm25",
   "health_impact",
   "emissions",
   "ff10",
   "nei2016",
   "zarr",
   "lambert_conformal",
   "reprojection",
   "data_loader",
   "variable_map",
   "referenced-component"
  ],
  "references": [
   {
    "citation": "Tessum, C.W., Hill, J.D., Marshall, J.D. (2017). InMAP: A model for air pollution interventions. PLoS ONE 12(4): e0176131.",
    "doi": "10.1371/journal.pone.0176131"
   },
   {
    "citation": "InMAP ISRM tutorial (2022-12-15).",
    "url": "https://inmap.run/blog/2022/12/15/tutorial/"
   }
  ],
  "x_esd": {
   "note": "Single-document pipeline. The loaders declare their own ingest; the model states the physics. Per emission record: LCC projection -> rectangle spatial join onto its source cell -> ASME plume rise at that cell's meteorology -> the SR emission layer its plume reaches -> the per-(cell, layer) emission binning -> fifteen gated SR contractions -> concentrations, PM2.5 and deaths. The InMAP source-receptor tutorial (https://inmap.run/blog/2019/04/20/sr/) reports 6928.959583 deaths (Krewski) and 15623.924632 (Lepeule) with plume rise; emitting everything at ground level instead gives 7524.918845602511 / 16979.632171487083, and the ~8% gap IS the plume rise. This document is not bug-compatible with InMAP's high-plume source-index defect (see `plume_layer`), so it is expected to land near, not on, the published pair.",
   "phase2_pushdown_DRAFT": {
    "summary": "HISTORICAL. A draft of the projection pushdown, kept as provenance: what it asks Phase-2-core for has since landed, and the single `ISRM_SR` loader it names has since been split into ISRM_Grid + ISRM_SR_L0/L1/L2 so each SR emission layer can be gated on its own. Read the loaders and `metadata.x_esd.pushdown` (written by the rewrite at run time) for what is actually true. DRAFT projection-pushdown variant of isrm.esm. The runner pre-pass that computed `ppl` (the distinct emission-bearing source cells) is replaced by an in-.esm value-invention producer aggregate `emis_src_cells_faq` (kind:derived index set emis_src_cells). This document will NOT validate or build until Phase-2-core lands the engine support listed below; it is authored as correct as the schema allows and modelled on tests/valid/geometry/bin_skolem_spatial_join.esm + conservative_regrid_overlap_join.esm.",
    "requires_phase2_core": {
     "lcc_at_build_time": "The overlap-gate producer reads the LCC-PROJECTED emission coords X/Y (and the full-grid cell rectangles W/S/E/N) as build-time const factors (index(X,r)/index(Y,r)/index(W,c).. must resolve in materialize_value_invention's const_arrays, value_invention.jl:388). Today the ONLY build-time path into those const_arrays is (a) caller-supplied kwd[:const_arrays] (build.jl:2469) and (b) _derive_binning_coords (build.jl:2476), which materialises via _materialize_geom_array -> _geo_compile, the LIMITED geometry vocabulary that EXCLUDES trig/exp/log/fn/apply_expression_template (geometry_setup.jl:588-604,630-639). X/Y are lambert_conformal_forward_x/y (an apply_expression_template that expands to trig), so _derive_binning_coords cannot evaluate them; _vi_eval has no trig either (value_invention.jl:327-362). The general-eval materialiser _materialize_setup_general_map (geometry_setup.jl:649-662) DOES speak trig/fn via _eval_cellwise but runs inside build_evaluator (build.jl:1350/1388) AFTER materialize_value_invention (build.jl:2485), so its output never reaches value-invention. SMALLEST FIX: route _derive_binning_coords' seed materialisation (geometry_setup.jl:1247) through _materialize_setup_general_map when _body_needs_general_eval(e), threading the model's registered_functions in; then a vi-index-target coordinate observed whose body is the LCC fn/template is evaluated at build time and fed to value-invention. ALTERNATIVE (works today, no engine change): the caller supplies X and Y (and the full-grid cell rectangles W/S/E/N) as const_arrays; the runner still does the cheap per-record LCC projection but the engine does the expensive spatial-join + distinct that invents ppl.",
     "members_fed_back_as_factor": "The producer's vi.members (the invented full-grid source-cell ids, materialize_value_invention's `members` return, value_invention.jl:948-950) must be fed back into the const-array factor `src_cell_of_ppl` (shape [emis_src_cells]) so cell_W/S/E/N = index(W, index(src_cell_of_ppl, c)) can gather the compact rectangles. Today materialize_value_invention returns members/extents but nothing wires members into a named model factor; Phase-2-core must bind vi.members[emis_src_cells_faq] -> const_arrays[\"src_cell_of_ppl\"] before build_evaluator consumes the model.",
     "gated_provider_deferral": "data_loaders.ISRM_SR.gated_select gates the SR source axis by the DERIVED set emis_src_cells (see that loader). The provider load must be DEFERRED until value-invention has materialised emis_src_cells (extent + member order), then deliver SR pre-sliced to the compact [emis_src_cells, rcv_cells] slab. Replaces the runner's lazy_select ([0], ppl, :) (G2). No engine field consumes gated_select today."
    }
   },
   "format_gaps": {
    "G1": "0.8.0 source schema has no `format` field / no .zarray pinning; recorded in loader x_esd.",
    "G2": "No lazy source-dim selection in-format. CLOSED for this model by the per-axis `gated_select` vocabulary: ISRM_SR_L0/L1/L2 each gate the SR source axis by the DERIVED set emis_src_cells and fix the emission layer to their own index, so the provider is deferred until value invention has materialised that set and then delivers the compact [emis_src_cells, rcv_cells] slab. The sibling half - the src-cell rectangles as the [0:N_SRC] prefix of the full grid - is CLOSED by the `range` axis of the same vocabulary (esm-spec 8.9.2): src_W/src_S/src_E/src_N are declared `select` ranges over the SAME on-disk arrays as W/S/E/N.",
    "G3": "CLOSED (esm-spec 8.9). FF10/zip semantics ARE expressible now: EGU_Emis declares `reader_options` (the *egu* member glob + the asserted header row), a `codes` map on `pollutant` (POLID text -> the pathway enum, an unrecognised code DROPS the record) and a `record_filter` (a record with no coordinate or no annual total is not a record). The runner no longer reads, maps or filters this table.",
    "G5": "No polygon/choropleth plot type; best available is a centroid scatter (see examples).",
    "G6": "CLOSED (esm-spec 8.9.4). N_REC is still runtime-discovered (default 0), but the LOADER discovers it: EGU_Emis declares `extent: {metaparameter: N_REC}`, so prepare() samples it before it closes metaparameters and the surviving record count sizes emis_records. No caller counts rows. PUSHDOWN DRAFT: N_PPL is GONE \u2014 emis_src_cells is a derived index set whose extent is materialised from the emis_src_cells_faq producer (value-invention).",
    "G8": "`unit_conversion` on a data-loader variable (esm-spec 8.2) is PARSED and VALIDATED by all three bindings and APPLIED by none of them: `providers_from_document` delivers the raw column, and nothing between the provider seam and the model touches it. Measured on the first 200 EGU records: max stkhgt 707.0 (feet, not the declared metres), max stktemp 1116.0 (degrees Fahrenheit, not kelvin). While the four stack columns were carried for fidelity and consumed by nothing, that was invisible; the moment plume rise reads them it is the difference between a stack in model layer 2 and one in model layer 4. So these four variables declare the unit their column actually arrives in, carry no `unit_conversion`, and the conversion is stated as the model observeds stk_height/stk_diam/stk_temp/stk_vel. A binding that starts applying `unit_conversion` will therefore not double-convert.",
    "G9": "A blank FF10 numeric field is delivered as NaN. `record_filter` cannot express \"blank means zero\" - `require_finite` only DROPS the record, and a stack with no recorded exit velocity is still a real emission record that InMAP reads with Go's zero value. So the stk_* observeds guard each column with `ifelse(x == x, ., 0)`, which is false only for NaN. Unguarded, one NaN propagates through the whole ASME branch tree and silently lands that record in SR layer 0.",
    "G7": "The two repeated bodies here \u2014 the meteorology gather and the layered emission binning \u2014 are written out at each of their 7 and 15 sites rather than declared once as expression_templates (esm-spec 9.6). This is now a TIDINESS debt, not a format limit. It was a format limit: under reference-preserving round-trip the call site was still an `apply_expression_template` node when `desugar_pushdown` ran, so `_pd_find_ifelse_cond` found no containment ifelse in an E_* body, the binning went unrecognised, and the rewrite SILENTLY did not fire \u2014 no derived support set, no gate, and the whole SR matrix in the fetch plan. EarthSciAST feat/pushdown-sees-template-refs fixed that: the detector now decides on Expand(tree) while the rewrite still edits the call site, so a factored body is recognised exactly as its expansion would be. The second obstacle, that a registry body may not reference a name a coupling `variable_map` rewrites (`template_body_references_coupling_rewritten_variable`, which src_W/src_S/src_E/src_N and emis_annual all are), has a sanctioned answer that guard's own message gives: bind the value through the template params. Folding these sites into two templates is a document change nobody has made yet."
   },
   "grid_mapping": {
    "grid_mapping_name": "lambert_conformal_conic",
    "standard_parallel": [
     33.0,
     45.0
    ],
    "latitude_of_projection_origin": 40.0,
    "longitude_of_central_meridian": -97.0,
    "earth_radius": 6370997.0,
    "false_easting": 0.0,
    "false_northing": 0.0
   }
  }
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "N_SRC": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 52411,
   "description": "ISRM source cells (first-52411 coarse subset of the InMAP grid)."
  },
  "N_RCV": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 52411,
   "description": "ISRM receptor cells (== the source grid, same ordered cell set)."
  },
  "N_ALL": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 596444,
   "description": "Every cell of the full InMAP grid: 8 ground layers of N_SRC cells plus 19 coarse layers of 9324, laid out layer-major. The length of W/S/E/N/TotalPop/MortalityRate and of the eight meteorology arrays (the zarr's `allcells` dimension)."
  },
  "N_LAYER": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 3,
   "description": "SR emission layers. All three are used: plume rise assigns every emission record to one of them (`plume_layer`), and the sibling loaders ISRM_SR_L0/L1/L2 fix this axis to 0, 1 and 2."
  },
  "N_REC": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 0,
   "description": "EGU FF10 point-source record count (runtime-discovered; G6)."
  }
 },
 "index_sets": {
  "src_cells": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "N_SRC"
  },
  "rcv_cells": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "N_RCV"
  },
  "all_cells": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "N_ALL"
  },
  "emis_layer": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "N_LAYER"
  },
  "pathways": {
   "kind": "categorical",
   "members": [
    "SOA",
    "pNO3",
    "pNH4",
    "pSO4",
    "PrimaryPM25"
   ]
  },
  "emis_records": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": "N_REC"
  }
 },
