    "stk_height": {
     "type": "observed",
     "units": "m",
     "shape": [
      "emis_records"
     ],
     "expression": {
      "op": "aggregate",
      "output_idx": [
       "r"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "r": {
        "from": "emis_records"
       }
      },
      "args": [
       "stkhgt"
      ],
      "expr": {
       "op": "ifelse",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "==",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "stkhgt",
            "r"
           ]
          },
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "stkhgt",
            "r"
           ]
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "*",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "stkhgt",
            "r"
           ]
          },
          0.3048
         ]
        },
        0.0
       ]
      }
     },
     "description": "Stack height in metres, from the raw FF10 column (col 17, feet). TWO conditionings, both measured against the delivered arrays rather than assumed. (a) UNITS: the loader variable declares its FF10 column's own unit and NO `unit_conversion` \u2014 see format gap G8; the conversion is stated here, at the one place the value is read, so it happens exactly once whatever a binding does at the provider seam. (b) BLANKS: a blank FF10 numeric field is delivered as NaN, and `record_filter` does not drop those records because a stack without this column is still a real emission record. InMAP reads the same blank as Go's zero value, so `ifelse(x == x, ., 0)` \u2014 false only for NaN \u2014 reproduces that. Left unguarded a single NaN would propagate through the whole branch tree and silently land the record in SR layer 0."
    },
