     "description": "Plume rise above the stack top, ctessum/atmos calcDeltaHPrecomputed branch for branch: momentum-dominated when Ts-Ta < 50 K and u < vs and vs > 10 m/s; otherwise buoyant, stable (29 (F/S1)^(1/3) u^(-1/3)) when SClass > 0.5 and S1 != 0, unstable (7.4 (F h^2)^(1/3) u^-1) otherwise, and 0 when F <= 0. THREE spellings here are load-bearing and were each shown necessary against all three bindings. (1) The cube-root exponent is the literal 0.333333333, not 1/3 \u2014 InMAP hard-codes it \u2014 and the power operator must be spelled `^`: Rust rejects `pow`/`**` as unlowered, while Julia and Python silently accept `pow`, so a typo would pass two bindings and fail the third. (2) EVERY fractional-power base is wrapped in max(., 0). `ifelse` is eager inside an aggregate everywhere, so the untaken branch is evaluated too, and on a negative base Julia raises DomainError, Rust yields NaN, and Python returns the REAL PART of a complex result behind a ComplexWarning \u2014 a plausible wrong number, the worst of the three. The clamp is a no-op on the branch actually taken. (3) `s_param == 0` is tested by NESTING rather than by an `and`, which reproduces Go's three-way stable guard (sClass > 0.5 && s1 != 0 && F > 0) exactly."
    },
