     "description": "THE ANSWER PLUME RISE EXISTS TO PRODUCE: which of the SR matrix's three emission layers each record's plume reaches. findLayer again, now on the plume height, with two InMAP rules folded in. A record with stack height 0 never enters IsPlumeIn at all (`if e.Height != 0` in sr.Reader.Concentrations) and emits at ground level, hence the outer ifelse. And min(., 2) IS the SR-layer clamp: sr.layers is [0,1,2], so layerFracs returns the matching layer for 0/1/2 and the topmost layer for anything above \u2014 model layers 3..26 all clamp to 2. Three indicators plus that clamp therefore need no separate model-layer variable. NOTE, deliberately not bug-compatible with InMAP: InMAP clamps a plume above model layer 7 to SR layer 2 but pairs it with an index built in the coarse 9324-cell high-grid, which it then reads against the 52411-cell ground grid, charging those emissions to the wrong source cell (654 records, 0.43% of mass, on this inventory). This document clamps to SR layer 2 at the cell the emission actually came from."
    },
